{{Short description|Football tournament}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group D of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] began on 11 June and completed on 21 June 2006.<ref>{{cite web |last=Saaid |first=Hamdan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2006full.html |title=World Cup 2006 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=7 February 2007 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> [[Portugal national football team|Portugal]] won the group, and advanced to the round of 16 (for the first time since [[1966 FIFA World Cup|1966]]), along with [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]]. [[Angola national football team|Angola]] and [[Iran national football team|Iran]] failed to advance.

